.TH tensor-wasm-deploy 1  "tensor-wasm-deploy "
.SH NAME
tensor\-wasm\-deploy \- Upload a Wasm module to a TensorWasm server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtensor\-wasm deploy\fR \fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFILE\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the file, base64\-encodes the bytes, and POSTs \fB{ "name": ..., "wasm_b64": ... }\fR to \fB{server}/functions\fR. On success the server\-assigned identifier is printed to stdout. On any non\-2xx response the structured error envelope is rendered as a human\-readable error and the process exits non\-zero.
.PP
The on\-wire body is capped at 64 MiB so a misconfigured path cannot silently OOM the CLI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR=\fISERVER\fR
Base URL of the target TensorWasm server (e.g. \fBhttp://localhost:8080\fR). Must use \fBhttp://\fR or \fBhttps://\fR and have a non\-empty host.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR=\fINAME\fR
Tenant\-supplied display name. Defaults to the file stem when omitted.
.TP
\fB\-\-tenant\fR=\fITENANT\fR [default: 0]
Tenant id to advertise on outbound API requests.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIFILE\fR]
Path to the \fB.wasm\fR file to deploy.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBTENSOR_WASM_TOKEN\fR
Bearer token attached as \fBAuthorization: Bearer ...\fR on the outbound request when set.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
tensor\-wasm(1), tensor\-wasm\-invoke(1)
